## Standards

### Component Rules
1. One component per file
2. Components are functional (no class components)
3. Props validated with default values where applicable
4. All interactive elements have unique `id` attributes
5. No inline styles — CSS Modules only

### UI/UX Rules
1. Donation action must be completable in ≤ 3 clicks
2. Mobile responsive — works on 360px+ screens
3. All form inputs have visible labels (not just placeholders)
4. Error messages appear inline below the invalid field
5. Loading states visible for all async operations
6. Empty states have helpful messages (not blank screens)
7. Focus states visible for keyboard navigation
8. Touch targets minimum 44x44px on mobile

### Performance Rules
1. Donation page: SSR (SEO + fast load)
2. Admin panel: CSR (auth-gated, no SEO needed)
3. Images use Next.js `<Image>` with optimization
4. No unnecessary client-side JavaScript on public pages
5. Lazy load admin components
6. Debounce search input (300ms)

### Accessibility Rules
1. Semantic HTML (`<main>`, `<nav>`, `<section>`, `<form>`)
2. Proper heading hierarchy (single `<h1>` per page)
3. Form inputs linked to labels via `htmlFor`
4. ARIA labels on icon-only buttons
5. Color contrast ratio ≥ 4.5:1 (WCAG AA)
6. Keyboard navigable (Tab, Enter, Escape)

